From: Matias Affolter <matiasaffolter@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:14:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Copy detection with PAPH 4.2: fingerprint index, comparator
 42, /copies API
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A new "paph" enrichment stage hashes each artwork with the PAPH 4.2 engine
(WebAssembly, vendored under vendor/paph with provenance) and indexes it in
PaphIndex, a SQLite-backed Durable Object that keeps the wires, an inverted
index of exact-match keys (Tier-1 local codes, descriptor bands, document
frequencies) and runs comparator 42 next to them. A new work is checked
against everything indexed before it: candidates come from both key families
(IDF-scored, top K each), pHash neighbours, the stored SigLIP vector's
neighbours and previous partners; once embed computes the image's vector, a
second pass checks that vector's neighbours. The screen-gated comparator
decides, 64 candidates at a time; verdicts land in D1 paph_matches as
(earlier, later) by chain time, with the comparator and calibration identity.

Robustness: the stage runs right after stats, before the AI stages' PNG
work; images over the hashing budget (768², ~37 MB of the hasher's ~60 B/px)
are divided (exact blow-ups) or box-filtered to fit; a check replaces the
verdicts of exactly the pairs it examined, in one transaction with
artworks.paph_hash, and writes a verdict only while both images are the ones
it was reached on and both posts are live, so concurrent checks can neither
erase nor resurrect each other's findings; a changed image withdraws its old
verdicts first; transient failures retry the message; unreadable stored wires
are marked for re-hashing, not fatal.

API: GET /copies/:id (stored verdicts, D1 only; live=1 with the admin
token), POST /copies-by-image (cached per image before any work), GET
/copies/:a/report/:b (the full evidence report, cached per image pair;
wires=1 adds both fingerprints so anyone can reproduce it), GET /paph/:id;
the two on-demand routes share a per-client rate limit (PAPH_LIMITER).
Admin: /admin/paph, /admin/paph/alerts, /admin/paph/rekey. Search items gain
artwork.stages.paph.

Tests: test/paph.test.ts (real fixtures: mirrored, cropped, upscaled,
recoloured and pasted copies are Copy; the hashing budget; the store on
node:sqlite with query plans held to primary keys, batching, key-less
checks; verdict writes on a D1 shim, including concurrent checks and stale
or deleted partners) and test/e2e/paph-e2e.mjs, which runs the whole
pipeline in workerd against a mock chain, re-verifies a published report
with both engines and trips the rate limit.

