+# vendor/paph — PAPH 4.2 as WebAssembly
+
+The perceptual-fingerprint engine behind copy detection, vendored from the `paph` repository
+(`wasm/` directory) so the Worker builds without a registry dependency.
+
+| file | what |
+|---|---|
+| `paph.wasm` | the Rust reference compiled to `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with SIMD128, `wasm-opt -O3` (526 kB, 196 kB gzipped) |
+| `paph.js` | hand-written ES-module glue over the module's C ABI (ABI 2): `init`, `Engine.hash/prepare/compare/screen/rank/indexKeys` |
+| `paph.d.ts` | its types |
+
+Provenance: `@pixagram/paph` 4.2.3, commit `3484423` (wire version 3, comparator 42,
+CAL-004-PROPOSED, KEYS_VERSION 1, ABI 2). The build is reproducible: `npm run build:wasm` at
+that commit, with the same toolchain (Rust 1.97, binaryen 132), writes the same bytes.
+
+```
+sha256  30f1439d25f78e3f033601fa34e9e077046c9d6003688a853fcbcbbf903eb16f  paph.wasm
+sha256  8614bae7efe3209381bc420f863878f6f1e5ccee3cefe6f548cfe28ac9b106c8  paph.js
+sha256  186f545a6d5d7c147e4f82118addfbb4175fde24cd6aea4f8c669d8c3a952849  paph.d.ts
+```
+
+The module is byte-for-byte equivalent to the native build and to the JavaScript engine
+(`paph-js`): the same pixels hash to the same wires and the same pair of wires gives the same
+report, key for key. That is what lets the API publish wires and reports that anyone can
+re-check in a browser.
+
+## Updating
+
+Copy `wasm/paph.js`, `wasm/paph.wasm` and `wasm/paph.d.ts` from a paph checkout (after
+`npm run build:wasm` there), update the hashes and commit above, run `npm test` and
+`npm run e2e:paph`. If the new release bumps `KEYS_VERSION`, deploy and call
+`POST /admin/paph/rekey` until `remaining` is 0 — keys are re-derived from the stored wires,
+no image is re-hashed. If it bumps the wire version, re-run the `paph` stage instead
+(`scripts/admin.sh reindex-all '"paph"' true`).
+
+Workers cannot compile WebAssembly from bytes at run time: the entry point imports
+`paph.wasm` as a module (Wrangler's `CompiledWasm` rule) and registers it with
+`setPaphModule()` in `src/paph/engine.ts`.
